Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: define fullcone for IPv6 masquerading

The shared masquerade template requires a fullcone argument after adding
Broadcom fullcone mode. Pass false for IPv6 since masquerade fullcone is
IPv4-only; IPv6 fullcone uses the separate zone-fullcone template.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---

--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
@@ -353,7 +353,7 @@
 {%   if (zone.masq6 && !fw4.default_option("fullcone6")): %}
 {%    for (let saddrs in zone.masq6_src_subnets): %}
 {%     for (let daddrs in zone.masq6_dest_subnets): %}
-		{%+ include("zone-masq.uc", { fw4, zone, family: 6, saddrs, daddrs }) %}
+		{%+ include("zone-masq.uc", { fw4, zone, family: 6, saddrs, daddrs, fullcone: false }) %}
 {%     endfor %}
 {%    endfor %}
 {%   endif %}
